/// Twenty-five more pages of season 17, episodes 44 to 69.
///
/// The second half of that season, and it holds up: about two questions in
/// three survive the filter here, the same rate as the first batch and
/// twice what the later seasons gave.
///
/// Episode 46 would not load, twice, so episode 44 stands in its place and
/// the count of pages is still twenty-five.
///
/// Seven pages were wrong. Five are dropped and two kept with the fault
/// put right:
///
///   * one asked which of four cities lies furthest north and answered
///     Dehradun, when Shimla among its own options is further north.
///   * one gave the wrong winner of a football league and one the wrong
///     winner of a hockey final.
///   * one asked which cricketer has a Test double century and answered a
///     player who has none, while another option does.
///   * one named a golfer as a Deaflympics champion in a games where the
///     sport was not held.
///   * three mislabelled their own answer: the right name against the
///     wrong letter, so the letter pointed at a different option.
///   * one asked for the creature that fires a jet of bubbles from its
///     claw and keyed an option that is not an animal at all. The fact is
///     worth having, so it is here asking plainly for the pistol shrimp.
///   * one asked which organisation turned eighty in 2025. That is true
///     only in 2025, so it is here asking what it rests on: which body was
///     founded in 1945.
///
/// Answer positions cycle 0, 1, 2, 3.
